# Partita in A minor for solo flute, BWV 1013: Bourree angloise
# (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: an "English" bourree in 2/4: quick, witty, with crisp
# eighths, short sixteenth runs and leaps that imply a second voice.
# Light on its feet; the closing movement of the partita.
#
# Time signature: 2/4 with an eighth-note upbeat, 70 bars (A 1-20,
# B 21-70, each half entered on an upbeat). Mutopia file
# bwv1013-3.mid, the fourth score (Allemande, Corrente, Sarabande,
# Bourree): checked against bwv1013.ly. Both halves repeat in the score;
# the MIDI plays each once, so play writes them out.
#
# Range: D4 to D6, no notes lifted.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 112, 280 beats with repeats, about 2:30. I could not
# confirm a flautist's track time. Recital recordings in the Arizona
# State University library run 1:33 to 2:22 (with repeats, about 118 to
# 180), and a sheet-music site suggests 108. 112 is my judgment: lively,
# with the sixteenths at 8 frames each so the runs stay clean.
#
# Structure (score bars, my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   A  1-4    A minor, the tune.
#      5-10   C major, broken chords.
#      11-16  Sequence (B flat, F, F sharp, G).
#      17-20  Cadence in C major.
#   B  21-34  D minor and A, cadence in D minor (34).
#      35-46  Rising sequences, E minor, cadence (46).
#      47-54  Sequences, chromatic falling pairs (51-52), toward A minor.
#      55-58  The opening tune returns in A minor.
#      59-70  Chromatic pairs again (63-64), runs and the final cadence.
#
# Bars as performed (play): A 0.75-20.75, A repeat 20.75-40.75,
# B 40.75-90.75 (score x = x+20), B repeat 90.75-140.75 (score x = x+70).

pickup 8
tempo 112

play 0.75-20.75 0.75-20.75 20.75-70.75 20.75-70.75

dyn 1 f              # A first time
dyn 20.75 mp         # A repeat, an echo
dyn 40.75 f          # B first time
dyn 90.75 mp         # B repeat, an echo
dyn 125 f            # score 55: the tune returns, full to the end

rit 2 0.8            # the last two bars
